title: "pallet-vesting: migrate from LockableCurrency to fungible freezes"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `pallet-vesting` no longer uses the deprecated `Currency`/`LockableCurrency` traits for the
      vesting balance. The unvested balance is now held with a `fungible` freeze under
      `FreezeReason::Vesting`, and transfers/balance queries use the `fungible` traits. This is part
      of the `Currency` -> `fungible` migration effort (#226 / #12399).

      Config changes (breaking):
      - `type Currency` bound changes from `LockableCurrency` to
        `fungible::{Inspect + Mutate + MutateFreeze<Id = RuntimeFreezeReason> + InspectFreeze}`.
      - New `type RuntimeFreezeReason: From<FreezeReason>` must be supplied (the runtime's aggregated
        `RuntimeFreezeReason`). Runtimes must ensure their `pallet-balances` instance sets
        `FreezeIdentifier = RuntimeFreezeReason` and a sufficient `MaxFreezes`.
      - New `type OldCurrency: LockableCurrency + Currency<Balance = BalanceOf>` is retained to
        remove pre-existing vesting locks during migration and to back the legacy `VestingSchedule`
        / `VestedTransfer` trait implementations consumed by other pallets (claims, purchase,
        crowdloan). It is otherwise unused.
      - `type UnvestedFundsAllowedWithdrawReasons` is removed. Freezes are unconditional and have no
        per-`WithdrawReasons` equivalent (see behaviour note below).

      Migration is lazy: any `vest` / `vest_other` / `vested_transfer` / `merge_schedules`
      interaction converts an account's legacy lock to a freeze. A new permissionless
      `migrate_to_freeze(target)` extrinsic (call index 6) is provided to migrate dormant accounts.
  - audience: Runtime User
    description: |
      Existing vesting schedules are unaffected; the locked amount is moved from a lock to a freeze
      of the same amount on the account's next interaction with the pallet, or by anyone calling the
      new permissionless `migrate_to_freeze` extrinsic on the account.

      Behaviour change: previously a runtime could allow the unvested (locked) balance to still be
      used for the reasons configured in `UnvestedFundsAllowedWithdrawReasons` (e.g. paying
      transaction fees). With freezes this is no longer possible: the unvested balance is frozen for
      all purposes until it vests.

